The 12 parametrized tests in the QA file exercise `spawn` with both string and list `cmd` values, both `shell=False` and `shell=True`, both empty and custom `env`, missing binaries, and simulated `OSError` from `os.posix_spawnp`. In `libqtile.core.manager.spawn`, that means the suite covers the string branch (`1304`, `1305`), the list branch (`1307`, `1308`), the common setup (`1310`, `1311`), the shell rewrite (`1312`) for shell cases, the lookup check (`1314`) plus the missing-command early return (`1315`, `1316`), the empty-env copy/pop block (`1318`, `1319`, `1324`) and also the path that skips it when custom env is supplied, the `/dev/null` context and `file_actions` construction (`1327`-`1331`, `1334`), and both the normal spawn call and exception handler (`1341`-`1345`). The Python-3.13-only append inside the version guard is not required by the test logic, so it is not included.

## Answer
